{
  "description": "How extraction/measure_sections.mjs maps rendered DOM regions to section ids at 1440px. One representative route per route-set that together covers every section contract (a greedy cover of routes.json, so every section is measured at least once). Each entry names the START element of one section instance: path = child indexes (1-based, all children) below <main>; css + nth = the nth document-order match of a selector (the 1px-rule divider stack). The script tiles the page: a section runs from its start to the next section start (the last runs to the end of the document), so the measured heights always sum to the document height and include the margins between sections. continuation entries add their extent to the previous instance of the same section (a hero that wraps a customer banner). shell.header is the fixed header element and takes no page height; the footer runs to the end of the document. The route \"*\" is the fallback page and is requested as /page-not-built-yet/.",
